    (ROOT/"docs/hr-v0-j2-soft-contact-pad-p0.1.md").write_text(f"# HR-V0 J2 soft-contact pad P0.1\n\n> **{WARNING}**\n\nR275 names Rogers `2300327` / PORON `4790-92-25024-04P` as the preferred unselected test coupon. Its published 0.61 +/-0.08 mm thickness fits the current 0.75 mm envelope, but its compression data are not an energy- or stall-stop rating.\n\nThe current unaccepted inertia gives {e10:.9f} J at 10 deg/s. By contrast, the radius-basis endpoint force doing work through 0.75 mm gives {work:.9f} J, about {work/e10:.1f} times the kinetic energy. That comparison is deliberately an order-of-magnitude warning: exact contact-normal work and measured torque decay remain open. It proves why the metal backup must remain structural and why power-removal time dominates.\n\nACE `MC5M-3-B`, the smallest catalogued energy-rated comparator found, needs 4 mm stroke and a minimum listed impact speed about 59 times HR-V0's nominal 10 deg/s tangent speed; it is rejected for the current envelope.\n\n[Interactive pad guide](../release/hr-v0/j2-soft-contact-pad-p0.1/index.html)\n",encoding="utf-8")
